# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every variable here is OPTIONAL — with none of them set the
# app runs exactly as it always has: fully client-side, all state in localStorage.

# --- Supabase (multi-device sync) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Without these two the app is local-only: no account, no network, no sync.
# With them, every cook signs up, joins a restaurant with a 6-character code, and the whole
# AppState syncs in real time. See "Two modes, same app" in CLAUDE.md.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# --- Google Gemini (AI recipe scanning) ---------------------------------------------------
# Enables "photograph a recipe → structured draft" in the Recipes screen
# (src/lib/geminiScanner.ts). Without it that screen falls back to on-device OCR only
# (tesseract.js), which is what it did before this feature existed.
#
# ⚠ SECURITY: Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the built JavaScript. On a deployed
# site this key is PUBLIC — anyone who opens the bundle can read it and spend your quota.
# It is fine for local development. Before putting it in Vercel production, consider
# proxying the call through a server function so the key stays server-side, and restrict
# the key in Google AI Studio to the referrers you expect.
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
